<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Linggadjati Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1946–1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Linggarjati Agreement · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-national-revolution">Indonesian National Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Linggadjati Agreement was a settlement negotiated in November 1946 at Linggadjati near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-java">West Java</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, and signed in March 1947. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> recognised the Republic's de facto authority over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madura">Madura</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, and both sides agreed to form a federal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Indonesia within a Netherlands-Indonesian Union. Disputes over its meaning led to the first Dutch 'police action' in July 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/linggadjati-agreement.jpg" alt="Linggadjati Agreement" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Polygoon Hollands Nieuws (producent) / Nederlands Instituut voor Beeld en Geluid (beheerder) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%22LINGGADJATI%22_GETEKEND-PGM4011927.webm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
